# GitHub Recovery Rule

## Mission

Help transform my GitHub profile into a professional engineering portfolio.

## Working Principles

- Always analyze before changing anything.
- Explain recommendations before implementing them.
- Prefer creating documentation before code changes.
- Break work into small milestones.
- Keep commits focused and descriptive.

## GitHub Safety

- Never delete repositories automatically.
- Never archive repositories automatically.
- Never change repository visibility automatically.
- Never force-push.
- Always ask before any destructive action.

## Documentation

When completing a task:

1. Update the relevant document.
2. Keep the roadmap current.
3. Mark completed work.
4. Suggest the next logical task.

## Engineering Standards

- Prefer small commits.
- Prefer Issues before implementation.
- Keep README files concise.
- Improve documentation whenever appropriate.